# Laurium's test environment, never its image (ADR-135 Amendment 6): Python 3.13 with
# OspreyFlow_Core/services/laurium/requirements.txt installed by hash, then laurium_test_requirements.txt,
# compiled from this file with hashes and installed with --require-hashes --no-deps:
#
#   uv pip compile --python-version 3.13 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --only-binary :all: \
#     --generate-hashes -c OspreyFlow_Core/services/laurium/requirements.txt \
#     -o OspreyFlow_Build/tests/conformance/model_port/laurium_test_requirements.txt \
#     OspreyFlow_Build/tests/conformance/model_port/laurium_test_requirements.in
#
# What the Build suite's own conftest needs, and the Conduit code the tests reach: the review queue's
# store (`services.api.review`, asyncpg) for Laurium's findings reaching it `pending`. Versions are the
# Conduit lock's (OspreyFlow_Core/uv.lock), so both environments test with the same ones.
